{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":[],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Create one structured workout requested by the user, scheduled within the next 7 days. Stores a pending plan; does NOT immediately deliver to or start Apple Watch. The first delivery is manual: open telo on iPhone > Planned workouts and tap Schedule on Watch to grant permission. Afterwards the user may opt into automatic delivery for newly created plans on that iPhone. Background scheduling is opportunistic, not immediate; otherwise review each plan manually. Use seconds/meters and an explicit local UTC offset. definition.type picks the workout: custom (default: warmup, repeatable work/recovery blocks, cooldown), pacer (cover a distance in a set time; the Watch shows ahead/behind), single_goal (one goal for the whole session; the only way to set an active-calorie goal) or multisport (triathlon/duathlon legs). Each custom step may carry ONE alert (Apple Watch limit): heart_rate_range, heart_rate_zone (the Watch's zones 1-5), pace_range or pace_threshold (seconds per km or mi; e.g. 5:00-5:30/km = fastest_seconds 300, slowest_seconds 330), speed_range/speed_threshold (kph or mph), cadence_range/cadence_threshold, power_range/power_threshold (watts) or power_zone; metric average uses the step average instead of the current value. Support, from WorkoutKit: pace/speed for running and cycling; cadence and power for cycling and outdoor running only; power_zone for cycling only; walking, swimming, strength and the rest take heart-rate alerts only; distance goals for running, cycling, walking, hiking, swimming, wheelchair and outdoor rowing. Unsupported combinations are rejected here with the reason. Alerts, plan types other than custom and activities beyond running/cycling/walking/strength/functional_strength/hiit/swimming need telo 1.12+ on iPhone; next_step says when the user must update. Step names can describe reps/weights; these are instructions, not native repetition goals. Pool swimming uses activity=swimming and location=indoor only. Optional pool_length_m is displayed for review; the user sets pool length on Watch when starting because WorkoutKit has no pool-length setter. For a yard pool send distance_unit=yd (goals still in meters): the Watch then shows yards and matches its yard pool; meter goals in a yard pool make the Watch reconfigure the workout. pool_distance_with_time goals require meters and seconds, and advance only when BOTH distance and time are fulfilled (send-off intervals; overrunning distance delays the next step). Distance-only goals are also supported. Pool custom workouts require watchOS 11 or later. Device supportsActivity/supportsGoal validation can reject unsupported activities, goals or alerts before scheduling. Retry with the SAME idempotency_key and payload. Read workout_plans to check delivery and exact recorded results. Never claim the Watch received a pending plan.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"definition":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"activity":{"enum":["running","cycling","walking","strength","functional_strength","hiit","swimming","hiking","rowing","elliptical","stair_climbing","cross_training","core_training","mixed_cardio","dance","yoga","pilates","jump_rope","kickboxing","wheelchair_run","wheelchair_walk","other"],"type":"string"},"blocks":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"iterations":{"maximum":30,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"steps":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"purpose":{"enum":["work","recovery"],"type":"string"},"step":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"alert":{"description":"At most one alert per step (an Apple Watch limit). Prefer this over heart_rate_bpm.","oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"kind":{"const":"heart_rate_range","type":"string"},"max_bpm":{"maxim